BLOCK FB FB_ShredderSequencerStim
ROOTID 0
NUMBER 9004
LANGUAGE LAD
TITLE "Shredder Sequencer Stimulus Head"
COMMENT "Presents a commanded plant to FB_ShredderSequencer so a conformance index exercises the sequencer against equipment that behaves to order. NETWORKS 1-17 ARE GENERATED - they are the index shell emitted by Harness.Map.StimShellGenerator from this slot's declared spec, and they are mechanism: the index latch and clock, three head and three tail cleardown phases, the scenario, the reset request, the latched-cause check and the four outcomes it publishes, the observation window, completion and re-arm. NETWORKS 18-27 ARE AUTHORED, because each is a claim about the plant rather than mechanism - what the equipment does when the PLC commands it. Phase codes published as Stim.Phase are positional: 1 head disarm, 2 head reset, 3 head verify, 4 scenario, 5 tail disarm, 6 tail reset, 7 tail verify, 0 between indexes; never decode them against another head's. THE FEEDBACK MODEL IS CLOSED-LOOP AND THAT IS NOT A REFINEMENT: the shredder motor block latches a fail-to-run ten seconds after it commands a contactor that does not confirm, and that fault aborts three of the sequencer's step transitions, so a feedback timeline that ignored what the motor was actually commanded would inject aborts no vector asked for. Each modelled contactor answers the output the PLC is really driving, after a delay the vector chooses. THE FAULT RESET IS ARBITRATED, NOT DRIVEN: DB_Controls.FaultReset is one coil shared with the hopper head, the pusher head, the motor block and the pusher block, so the shell publishes a request and Network 19 passes another head's value through whenever this index is not running. Every test-injection member is written the same way, for the same reason. THE STALENESS QUESTION, ANSWERED: the sequencer's dwell timers all key on Step, which this head moves, so every one of them advances; its two staleness-sensitive elements do NOT - ReversalWindowTimer watches for the absence of new reversals and ReversalCount counts entries into Step 60 - and nothing this head can present will move either, because Step 60 is unreachable in the as-built block. That is a property of the block under test, not of this head, and it is recorded here so a green is never read as coverage of them. This head drives the sequencer's inputs and nothing else: it writes the input buffer's own test-injection members, the operator pusher mode, and the operator fault reset."

INTERFACE
  INPUT
  OUTPUT
  STATIC
    Stim : "UDT_ShredderSequencerStim" COMMENT "Caller interface. The harness copy layer writes the command members before an index and reads the published ones while it runs. Member comments live on the type, not repeated here, so the two cannot drift."
@@STIM_MEMBERS@@
    Running : Bool COMMENT "An index is under way: set by Start and held until the index reaches its end, so the harness dropping the start bool part-way through cannot truncate one and produce a short index that still looks complete."
    RunTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    RunT : Time COMMENT "Time since the index started, copied out of the index timer so every phase compares against a plain value."
    ScenT : Time COMMENT "Time since the scenario started, which is the instant the head cleardown finished. Every commanded event time is measured against this and never against the index clock."
    DisarmDwell : Time COMMENT "Length of each disarm phase."
    ResetDwell : Time COMMENT "Length of each reset phase, and therefore the width of the reset pulse inside it."
    VerifyDwell : Time COMMENT "Length of each verify phase - long enough that a latch which was going to re-assert has done so before the outcome is published."
    ResetPulseEnd : Time COMMENT "End of the in-scenario reset pulse under ResetMode 1."
    ResetPulse : Bool COMMENT "A cleardown reset phase is running."
    ScenarioReset : Bool COMMENT "The scenario's own commanded reset is asserted, whichever mode asked for it."
    CauseStanding : Bool COMMENT "Any latched cause the cleardown has to clear is standing right now."
    InHeadDisarm : Bool
    InHeadReset : Bool
    InHeadVerify : Bool
    InScenario : Bool
    InTailDisarm : Bool
    InTailReset : Bool
    InTailVerify : Bool
    HeadDisarmEnd : Time
    HeadResetEnd : Time
    HeadEnd : Time
    ScenarioEnd : Time
    TailDisarmEnd : Time
    TailResetEnd : Time
    TailEnd : Time
    Disarmed : Bool COMMENT "The index is running and the scenario is not - every cleardown phase, head and tail. THIS IS THE DISARM LEVER: while it is true the plant is held stopped at Step 0 and every fault source is held clear, so no cleardown can be defeated by a cause being re-created underneath it."
    StartPressEnd : Time COMMENT "When the commanded cycle-start press ends, so the press window compares against a single time instead of adding one inside a condition."
    StopFired : Bool COMMENT "The scenario has reached its commanded stop instant. WHICH stop it is comes from the three levers, not from this."
    CmdCycleStart : Bool COMMENT "Commanded operator cycle-start button."
    CmdCycleStop : Bool COMMENT "Commanded operator cycle-stop button. Asserted through every cleardown phase as well, which is what holds the plant at Step 0 while the latches are being cleared."
    CmdDownstream : Bool COMMENT "Commanded downstream-running permission. Held true through the cleardown so the only stop reason there is the button, and a cleardown can never be mistaken for a downstream-loss scenario."
    CmdHealthy : Bool COMMENT "Commanded control-circuit healthy input. Held true through the cleardown for the same reason."
    CmdHopperHigh : Bool COMMENT "Commanded hopper high-level sensor."
    CmdMotorFault : Bool COMMENT "Commanded field motor-fault input."
    CmdRunFwdFB : Bool COMMENT "Modelled forward-running feedback - what the contactor is actually reporting back to the PLC."
    CmdRunRevFB : Bool COMMENT "Modelled reverse-running feedback."
    CmdDischargeRunning : Bool COMMENT "Modelled discharge-conveyor running feedback."
    FwdRespTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    RevRespTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    DischargeRespTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
  TEMP
  CONSTANT

